          <figure class="page-mascot page-mascot--parts" aria-hidden="true">
            <img src="{{ basePath | default('') }}static/image/any-icon/extension/parts.png" alt="" width="440" height="455"
              loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </figure>
          <h2>Overview</h2>
          <p class="parts-lede"><span class="i18n-en">This collection gathers the biological parts PAGER-Yeast contributed to the iGEM Registry. They cover the re-engineered <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> chassis, the humanised G-protein interface, the reporter that reads the pathway out, and the antigen-recognition module that gates the receptor; below they are listed the way the Registry itself classifies them, as basic parts and composite parts.</span></p>

          <p class="parts-tally">
            <span class="i18n-en">23 parts — 17 basic, 6 composite.</span>
          </p>

          <p class="parts-note"><span class="i18n-en">Every part number links to its Registry page, where the full sequence, annotations and any future characterisation data are kept.</span></p>
        </div>

        <!-- 分组依据：为什么按基础 / 复合分 -->
        <div id="parts-organisation" class="content-card">
          <h2>How this collection is organised</h2>
          <p class="parts-desc"><span class="i18n-en">Every entry below is one Registry part, and the two sections follow the Registry classification rather than the order of the experiments. Basic parts are single functional units — a guide sequence, a homology arm, the EYNLV swap, a promoter — that can be used on their own or recombined freely. Composite parts are assemblies of two or more basic parts, submitted so that a combination which is known to work can be taken as a single piece. Each composite entry lists what it is built from.</span></p>
          <p class="parts-tail"><span class="i18n-en">All four modules of the project are represented here: chassis engineering, <i>GPA1</i> humanisation, the reporter system, and the antigen-recognition module that gates the receptor.</span></p>
        </div>

        
        <div id="parts-basic" class="content-card parts-group" data-group="basic">
          <h2>Basic Parts</h2>
          <p class="parts-desc"><span class="i18n-en">The single units this project is built from — 17 parts, each usable on its own or as the building block of one of the composites below.</span></p>

          <div class="parts-head" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="parts-head__cell"><span class="i18n-en">Part ID</span></span>
            <span class="parts-head__cell"><span class="i18n-en">Name</span></span>
            <span class="parts-head__cell"><span class="i18n-en">Type</span></span>
            <span class="parts-head__cell"><span class="i18n-en">Length</span></span>
            <span class="parts-head__cell"><span class="i18n-en">Function</span></span>
          </div>

          <ul class="parts-sheet">
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-267zce19" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-267zce19" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_267ZCE19</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en">SpCas9 sgRNA scaffold (pML104)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Non-coding RNA</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">79<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">The constant 79 bp scaffold of the SpCas9-compatible sgRNA used in the pML104 CRISPR-Cas9 system. It supplies the structured RNA region that lets the sgRNA fold and bind SpCas9; it does not decide which locus gets cut.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Chimeric sgRNA scaffold taken from the pML104 CRISPR-Cas9 system.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-262tzxv3" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-262tzxv3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_262TZXV3</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>FAR1</i>-targeting guide sequence (crRNA_FAR1_KO_up)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Guide RNA</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">20<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">A 20 bp guide sequence aimed at the <i>FAR1</i>/YJL157C locus of <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> BY4741. It carries the targeting information for a pML104-based SpCas9 sgRNA cassette, so a <i>FAR1</i> knockout needs nothing beyond this spacer plus the shared scaffold; the adjacent TGG PAM sits outside the part and is not included here. <i>FAR1</i> encodes the cell-cycle inhibitor that arrests G1 after pheromone stimulation, which is why removing it keeps the strain dividing through a long fluorescence read-out.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Designed in CRISPOR and picked on predicted on-target scores together with off-target analysis.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26hn2w3g" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26hn2w3g" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26HN2W3G</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>FAR1</i> homology repair template (4 bp deletion, PAM mutated)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Engineered region</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">1142<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">The donor that repairs <i>FAR1</i> once Cas9 has cut it. It carries 4 bp missing (CACT) inside the guide site GCGTCACGATCTCCACTTGG and a PAM changed from TGG to TAG, so the repaired chromosome is no longer recognised by the same guide. The short deletion shifts the reading frame and knocks the gene out; the PAM edit is the safeguard against a second cut. No foreign sequence and no selection marker are introduced, so the chassis stays marker-free apart from later integration steps.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en"><i>S. cerevisiae</i> <i>FAR1</i> locus, modified with a 4 bp deletion and a PAM mutation on top of the CRISPR target GCGTCACGATCTCCACTTGG.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-2658b1za" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-2658b1za" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_2658B1ZA</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>SST2</i>-targeting guide sequence (crRNA_SST2_KO)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Guide RNA</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">20<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">The <i>SST2</i> counterpart of the <i>FAR1</i> guide: 20 bp aimed at the <i>SST2</i> locus of <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> BY4741 and used the same way in a pML104 sgRNA cassette. <i>SST2</i> is the principal negative regulator of mating-pheromone signalling, so taking it out is what lifts the ceiling on how strongly the pathway can respond. The CGG PAM next to this target is not part of the part.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Designed computationally with a CRISPR design tool and selected for SpCas9 knockout in the pML104 system.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-262sr0ed" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-262sr0ed" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_262SR0ED</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>SST2</i> homology repair template (4 bp deletion, PAM mutated)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Engineered region</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">989<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">The donor that repairs <i>SST2</i> once Cas9 has cut it, mirroring the <i>FAR1</i> template: 4 bp missing (TCTG) inside the target site TCGCCACGAGTTCTGTCCTG, and the adjacent PAM changed from CGG to CAG so the repaired locus is no longer a valid target. The deletion shifts the reading frame and knocks the gene out; the PAM edit makes a second cut unlikely. Nothing foreign and no selection marker are introduced.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en"><i>S. cerevisiae</i> <i>SST2</i> locus, modified with a 4 bp deletion and a PAM mutation on top of the CRISPR target TCGCCACGAGTTCTGTCCTG.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26hubyay" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26hubyay" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26HUBYAY</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>GPA1</i> upstream homology arm</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Homologous region</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">500<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">500 bp taken from directly upstream of <i>GPA1</i>/YHR005C. Its only job is to be recognised: <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> recombines where the sequence matches, so this arm is what delivers the replacement to the right place on chromosome VIII. It pairs with the downstream arm to bracket the region being rewritten.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">The <i>GPA1</i>/YHR005C locus on chromosome VIII of <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> S288C.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26eg2lor" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26eg2lor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26EG2LOR</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>GPA1</i> C-terminal Gαq-derived EYNLV sequence with stop codon</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Engineered region</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">18<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">The 18 bp at the centre of the swap: five Gαq-derived residues, EYNLV, followed by a stop codon. The C-terminus of a Gα protein is what decides which receptor it can work with, so replacing the yeast KIGII with this sequence is the whole point of the humanisation step. The design follows the Gαq chimera reported by Komatsuzaki and colleagues (1997).</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Designed from the C-terminal five-residue Gαq chimera reported by Komatsuzaki et al. (1997); C-terminal sequence of <i>Homo sapiens</i> GNAQ (Gαq).</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26yeukxx" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26yeukxx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26YEUKXX</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>GPA1</i> downstream homology arm</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Homologous region</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">500<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">500 bp from the region downstream of <i>GPA1</i>/YHR005C, closing the other side of the target. Together with the upstream arm it defines exactly which stretch of the locus is replaced, so the edited allele carries the humanised C-terminus and nothing else from the original sequence.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">The genomic region downstream of the <i>GPA1</i>/YHR005C locus on chromosome VIII of <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> S288C.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26j53mf4" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26j53mf4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26J53MF4</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>FUS1</i> promoter (435 bp)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Promoter</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">435<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">A 435 bp fragment of the <i>FUS1</i> upstream region from <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> S288C. <i>FUS1</i> is one of the genes the mating pathway switches on, which makes its promoter a convenient readout: whatever activates the cascade upstream ends up written out here as transcription. This part is the promoter only — no reporter, no terminator, no backbone — so it can be paired with whichever output a construct needs.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en"><i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> S288C chromosome III, NCBI RefSeq NC_001135.5, positions 71,368–71,802 on the forward strand.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-266cqi7l" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-266cqi7l" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_266CQI7L</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>S. cerevisiae</i> α-factor pre-signal peptide</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Signal peptide</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">57<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">The pre-region of the <i>S. cerevisiae</i> α-factor precursor, used as an N-terminal signal peptide to route a downstream fusion protein into the secretory pathway. In the PAGER receptor designs it carries the extracellular sensing module toward the plasma membrane, so the antigen-binding domain ends up facing the outside of the cell.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Derived from the <i>S. cerevisiae</i> α-factor (<i>MFα1</i>) pre-sequence.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26di50c2" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26di50c2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26DI50C2</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en">Ste2 antagonist peptide CRGPQLKPGQPMY</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Polypeptide</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">39<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">Encodes the 13-residue Ste2 antagonist peptide CRGPQLKPGQPMY, designed from structure–activity studies of the α-factor–Ste2 interaction. It is the auto-inhibitory element of the PAGER-Ste2 design: without H1N1 HA it occupies the Ste2 ligand-binding region and suppresses basal signalling, and antigen binding to the fused nanobody is expected to relieve that inhibition.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Sequence taken from published structure–activity studies of α-factor analogues (doi:10.1128/MCB.16.9.4700; doi:10.1016/j.peptides.2003.11.028).</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26j0ywr7" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26j0ywr7" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26J0YWR7</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en">Flexible Gly-Ser linker (11 aa)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Polypeptide</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">33<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">A flexible Gly-Ser-rich linker placed between the extracellular regulatory module and hM1Dq. It gives the two domains conformational freedom and enough spatial separation to fold independently, while keeping steric interference with receptor function low.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Synthetic Gly-Ser linker, 11 residues.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26u5ou4i" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26u5ou4i" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26U5OU4I</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en">Anti-H1N1 HA nanobody</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Coding sequence</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">342<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">A single-domain antibody that specifically recognises the haemagglutinin of influenza A H1N1. In the PAGER receptor it sits in the extracellular region and serves as the antigen-recognition module: HA binding is meant to relieve steric inhibition of the receptor and let the downstream pathway fire.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Nanobody raised against H1N1 haemagglutinin, codon-optimised for <i>S. cerevisiae</i>.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26i4t75i" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26i4t75i" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26I4T75I</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en">TEV protease cleavage site</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Protease site</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">21<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">A TEV protease recognition site placed between the extracellular antigen-binding module and the receptor-associated domain. Cleaving it removes the upstream module, so receptor activation can be tested with and without the antigen-gated half in place.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Standard TEV protease recognition sequence (ENLYFQG).</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-2624trua" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-2624trua" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_2624TRUA</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en">ALFA-tag (13-aa epitope)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Tag</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">39<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">Encodes the 13-residue ALFA-tag, an epitope recognised by ALFA-specific antibodies and binding reagents. In the PAGER receptor it sits between the TEV site and the flexible linker and is used to confirm that the fusion is expressed and reaches the membrane.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Synthetic ALFA epitope tag.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-266rb3hx" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-266rb3hx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_266RB3HX</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en">Muscarinic toxin 1 (MT1) auto-inhibitory domain</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Coding sequence</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">198<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">Muscarinic toxin 1, an extracellular auto-inhibitory domain used in the PAGERGq design. Fused to the N-terminus of hM1Dq it holds the receptor shut while no antigen is present; binding of the anti-H1N1 HA nanobody to its antigen is expected to relieve that block and let an orthogonal DREADD ligand activate hM1Dq.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Muscarinic toxin 1 from mamba venom, used here as a steric gate.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-267g8sjj" data-comp="basic">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-267g8sjj" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_267G8SJJ</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--basic">Basic part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en">Engineered hM1Dq receptor for yeast Gq signalling</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Coding sequence</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">1038<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">The engineered hM1Dq DREADD receptor adapted for expression in <i>S. cerevisiae</i>. It is the transmembrane signalling core of the PAGERGq system: once MT1-mediated auto-inhibition is relieved by antigen binding, it activates Gq-coupled signalling in response to an orthogonal DREADD ligand. The part carries the receptor modifications used in this project.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Engineered from the hM1Dq DREADD receptor for yeast expression.</span></p>

                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div id="parts-composite" class="content-card parts-group" data-group="composite">
          <h2>Composite Parts</h2>
          <p class="parts-desc"><span class="i18n-en">The 6 assembled entries. Each one is a combination of parts from the section above or from the wider Registry, and each lists its components.</span></p>

          <div class="parts-head" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="parts-head__cell"><span class="i18n-en">Part ID</span></span>
            <span class="parts-head__cell"><span class="i18n-en">Name</span></span>
            <span class="parts-head__cell"><span class="i18n-en">Type</span></span>
            <span class="parts-head__cell"><span class="i18n-en">Length</span></span>
            <span class="parts-head__cell"><span class="i18n-en">Function</span></span>
          </div>

          <ul class="parts-sheet">
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26ikmsko" data-comp="composite">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26ikmsko" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26IKMSKO</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--composite">Composite part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>FAR1</i> sgRNA expression cassette (SNR52p–guide–scaffold–SUP4t)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Engineered region</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">388<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">A complete expression cassette that puts the <i>FAR1</i> guide under RNA polymerase III control in yeast: the <i>SNR52</i> promoter drives transcription, the 20 bp spacer confers specificity, the SpCas9 scaffold supplies the RNA structure Cas9 binds, and the <i>SUP4</i> terminator ends the transcript. Together with the matching repair template it turns the target locus into a frameshift after a single Cas9 cut. The cassette is designed for the pML104 CRISPR-Cas9 system used throughout the chassis work.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Assembled from Registry parts plus a computationally designed <i>FAR1</i> spacer.</span></p>
                  <div class="part__construct">
                    <span class="part__construct-label">Construct</span>
                    <ol class="part__chain">
                        <li><a class="part__chip" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-k2926004" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_K2926004</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip part__chip--local" href="#parts-bba-262tzxv3">BBa_262TZXV3</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip part__chip--local" href="#parts-bba-267zce19">BBa_267ZCE19</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-k4278714" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_K4278714</a></li>
                    </ol>
                  </div>
                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26yvx4qt" data-comp="composite">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26yvx4qt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26YVX4QT</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--composite">Composite part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>SST2</i> sgRNA expression cassette (SNR52p–guide–scaffold–SUP4t)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Engineered region</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">388<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">The <i>SST2</i> twin of the <i>FAR1</i> sgRNA cassette, built from the same four Registry parts in the same order — <i>SNR52</i> promoter, <i>SST2</i> spacer, SpCas9 scaffold, <i>SUP4</i> terminator — for RNA polymerase III expression in yeast. Paired with the <i>SST2</i> repair template it gives a frameshift knockout after one Cas9 cut, and because the scaffold is shared with the <i>FAR1</i> cassette the two targets differ only in their 20 bp spacers.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Assembled from four Registry parts; the <i>SST2</i> spacer was designed computationally from the <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> <i>SST2</i> locus.</span></p>
                  <div class="part__construct">
                    <span class="part__construct-label">Construct</span>
                    <ol class="part__chain">
                        <li><a class="part__chip" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-k2926004" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_K2926004</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip part__chip--local" href="#parts-bba-2658b1za">BBa_2658B1ZA</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip part__chip--local" href="#parts-bba-267zce19">BBa_267ZCE19</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-k4278714" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_K4278714</a></li>
                    </ol>
                  </div>
                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-266k1vdv" data-comp="composite">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-266k1vdv" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_266K1VDV</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--composite">Composite part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>GPA1</i> C-terminal humanisation cassette with <i>URA3</i> selection marker</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Engineered region</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">2280<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">The complete donor cassette for editing <i>GPA1</i> in a single transformation. Running in order: the upstream homology arm, the humanised EYNLV sequence, the <i>URA3</i> promoter, the <i>URA3</i> gene, the <i>URA3</i> terminator, a short connecting sequence, and the downstream homology arm. In BY4741, which is <i>URA3</i> auxotrophic, the embedded <i>URA3</i> cassette is what lets transformants be recovered on uracil-deficient medium, while the flanking arms alone decide where the construct lands.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Assembled from BBa_26HUBYAY, BBa_26EG2LOR, BBa_K3939012, BBa_Y1007, BBa_K2407302, a custom linker and BBa_26YEUKXX.</span></p>
                  <div class="part__construct">
                    <span class="part__construct-label">Construct</span>
                    <ol class="part__chain">
                        <li><a class="part__chip part__chip--local" href="#parts-bba-26hubyay">BBa_26HUBYAY</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip part__chip--local" href="#parts-bba-26eg2lor">BBa_26EG2LOR</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-k3939012" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_K3939012</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-y1007" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_Y1007</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-k2407302" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_K2407302</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip part__chip--local" href="#parts-bba-26yeukxx">BBa_26YEUKXX</a></li>
                    </ol>
                  </div>
                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26d8d1sg" data-comp="composite">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26d8d1sg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26D8D1SG</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--composite">Composite part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en"><i>FUS1</i> promoter–<i>yEGFP</i> reporter fragment</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Engineered region</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">1152<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">A composite reporter that pairs the <i>FUS1</i> promoter with the <i>yEGFP</i> reporter CDS. The promoter answers to the yeast mating-response MAPK cascade, so once the pathway is active it drives <i>yEGFP</i> transcription and translation and the cell fluoresces green. It is the output module used to characterise both the re-engineered chassis and the humanised G-protein interface.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Assembled from the truncated <i>FUS1</i> promoter BBa_26J53MF4 and the <i>yEGFP</i> reporter CDS.</span></p>
                  <div class="part__construct">
                    <span class="part__construct-label">Construct</span>
                    <ol class="part__chain">
                        <li><a class="part__chip part__chip--local" href="#parts-bba-26j53mf4">BBa_26J53MF4</a></li>
                        <li><a class="part__chip" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-k3221207" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_K3221207</a></li>
                    </ol>
                  </div>
                </details>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="part" id="parts-bba-26yo211v" data-comp="composite">
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--id">
                <a class="part__id" href="https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26yo211v" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBa_26YO211V</a>
                <span class="part__badge part__badge--composite">Composite part</span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--name">
                <p class="part__name"><span class="i18n-en">PAGER-<i>STE2</i> H1N1 HA-gated yeast signalling module</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--type">
                <span class="part__type"><span class="i18n-en">Engineered region</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--len">
                <span class="part__len">623<span class="part__unit"> bp</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part__cell part__cell--fn">
                <p class="part__desc"><span class="i18n-en">The H1N1 HA-gated module that plugs into the native yeast Ste2 mating pathway. Reading N- to C-terminus it carries the α-factor pre-sequence, the Ste2 antagonist peptide, a flexible linker, the anti-H1N1 HA nanobody, a TEV site and an ALFA-tag. The nanobody provides HA recognition while the antagonist peptide gates Ste2 signalling; the Ste2 receptor itself is supplied by the chassis and is not part of this construct.</span></p>
                <details class="part__more">
                  <summary><span class="i18n-en">Source and composition</span></summary>
                  <p class="part__source"><span class="i18n-en">Assembled from BBa_266CQI7L, BBa_26DI50C2, BBa_26J0YWR7, BBa_26U5OU4I, BBa_26I4T75I and BBa_2624TRUA.</span></p>
                  <div class="part__construct">
